# Vercel upload ignore list.
#
# Vercel CLI uploads the project directory to build in the cloud. This file stops
# local-only material from leaving the machine.
#
# `.env.local` holds the Supabase service-role key, the session signing secret and
# the VAPID private key. Uploading it would copy production-grade secrets into the
# build. Production values are supplied as Vercel project environment variables
# instead. `.env.example` is the committed template and is safe to upload.

.env
.env.local
.env*.local

# Build and test output, regenerated on Vercel.
.next
out
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
.vercel

# Large local artefacts that are not part of the application.
*.tsbuildinfo